  "teaser": "The room where male soul voices stopped performing and started telling the truth - twelve tracks, no hiding.",
  "description": "There is a room in soul music that doesn't appear on any map. Not the dancefloor, not the church — somewhere between them, where a man sings something he cannot say straight out. That is where this show lives.\n\nWilliam Bell and Judy Clay listening to each other across a Memphis studio. Ronnie Dyson's falsetto sitting still rather than reaching. Curtis Mayfield setting down the weight for a moment. Bobby Womack talking to someone in the same room. Two Teddy Pendergrass tracks from the same year, the same label — completely opposite ends of himself.\n\nMinnie Riperton answers at the end. Because intimacy was always a conversation, not a monologue.\n\n— Simone",
  "quote": "In the Rain is a piano, some strings, and a man with nowhere left to hide. It's the most unguarded moment in this show. Let it land.",
  "home_quote": {
    "text": "The still ones are often the strongest. *He understood that earlier than most.*",
    "context": "On Luther Vandross, Better Love"
  },
